The Samurai is sort of like this already, except he kicks instead of using
his hands.  But if this *were* to be implemented, something would need to
be done to counterbalance the fact that he can't possibly have his weapon
rusted, damaged by a scroll, lost, cursed, etc.  Perhaps he can be restricted
to wearing no full-body armor whatsoever.  After all, Monks in AD&D, which
you quote as your source, can't do it either.  That would take this potential
new character class down a step or two, I'd say.  :)

